StudyForge original source, 2026.
The included gradle-wrapper.jar and standard gradlew.bat are from the Gradle
8.9.0 project, https://github.com/gradle/gradle, licensed Apache-2.0.
The POSIX gradlew here is a minimal original launcher.
Android, Kotlin, Python packages, FFmpeg and optional model weights retain
their respective licenses. No AI model weights are redistributed.

Optional video person segmentation uses separately obtained OpenCV Zoo PPHumanSeg
FP32 ONNX weights (PaddlePaddle Authors, Apache-2.0); weights are not bundled.
Source and license: https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/2027dd2f5a8a5746b5d4964900a0465afc6d3a53/models/human_segmentation_pphumanseg

Native phone person segmentation additionally uses ONNX Runtime 1.20.0 (MIT),
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime and its Swift Package Manager bindings.
No person-segmentation weights are bundled in the production app.
